{{- /*
layout.gohtml is the panel's outer frame: every page defines a "body" block and
is rendered inside this.

The body is not passed as a VALUE, it is defined as a BLOCK. Passed as a value,
the layout would have to convert it to template.HTML, and template.HTML DISABLES
escaping — in a panel that runs inside an administrator's session, disabling
escaping is the shortest path to handing an attacker admin privileges.

No template here uses template.HTML, template.JS or template.URL.

The navigation is rendered from a LIST the Go side supplies rather than written
out here, so a section added to the panel enters the menu by being added to that
list — and the current section is marked with aria-current, which is both what
the stylesheet keys on and what a screen reader announces. Two facts from one
source instead of two that can drift.
*/ -}}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ .Title }} · gobit</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ .StylesheetPath }}">
</head>
<body>
<header class="masthead">
  <span class="mark">gobit</span>
  <span class="role">admin</span>
  {{- if .Nav }}
  <nav aria-label="Sections">
    {{- range .Nav }}
    <a href="{{ .Path }}"{{ if .Current }} aria-current="page"{{ end }}>{{ .Label }}</a>
    {{- end }}
  </nav>
  {{- end }}
  {{- if .SignedIn }}
  <form class="spacer" method="post" action="{{ .LogoutPath }}">
    <button class="quiet" type="submit">Sign out</button>
  </form>
  {{- end }}
</header>
<main>
{{ template "body" . }}
</main>
</body>
</html>
